► **ANSWER**

**What was failing and why:**

The test `base-terminator-allows-dash-mode` invokes `new_chmod -- -w f`. After consuming `--`, the code sets `start = 2` and then unconditionally checks `argv[start][0] == '-'` to reject unknown options. This incorrectly rejects `-w` as an option even though `--` was supposed to end option processing and make `-w` the mode.

**What I changed:**

Only apply the "unknown option" rejection when `--` was *not* seen. I introduced a `saw_terminator` flag and guarded the dash check with it.

